Canonical LR(0) Collection Construction:
Augmented Grammar G':
(0) S' -> S
(1) S -> E
(2) E -> E + T
(3) E -> T
(4) T -> id

Construct Item Sets:
I0 = Closure({S' -> .S}) = {S' -> .S, S -> .E, E -> .E + T, E -> .T, T -> .id}
- Goto(I0, S) = I1: {S' -> S.} (Accept)
- Goto(I0, E) = I2: {S -> E., E -> E. + T}
- Goto(I0, T) = I3: {E -> T.}
- Goto(I0, id) = I4: {T -> id.}

From I2 on '+':
- Goto(I2, +) = I5: {E -> E + .T, T -> .id}
- From I5 on T: Goto(I5, T) = I6: {E -> E + T.}
- From I5 on id: Goto(I5, id) = I4 (already exists).

Total distinct LR(0) states = {I0, I1, I2, I3, I4, I5, I6} = 7 states.
Therefore, the canonical collection has exactly 7 states.

